---
# A gtest body is a long straight-line run of arrange/act/assert with no
# extracted helpers on purpose - a test that factors its own setup away stops
# reading as the specification it is. The check counts that shape as complexity
# and has no remedy for it that leaves the test readable.
Checks: '-readability-function-cognitive-complexity'
InheritParentConfig: true
# The static analyzer's default inlining mode, `dynamic-bifurcate`, forks every
# path at a virtual call whose receiver's dynamic type it cannot prove, once
# per candidate type. gtest's assertion macros put such calls in every
# EXPECT/ASSERT, so a test body multiplies its paths per assertion: measured on
# clang-tidy 19, import_parse_test.cpp spent 258 s of its 306 s in the analyzer
# and script_engine_test.cpp 560 s of its 604 s. `dynamic` still inlines a
# virtual call wherever the type is known and evaluates the rest without
# forking; the analyzer then takes 26 s on import_parse_test.cpp. The engine's
# own sources keep the default - they have no such fan-out (run_manager.cpp
# costs the same under either mode), so nothing is traded away there. The
# 155 test files were at zero analyzer findings in both modes when this was set.
#
# Set here rather than on the pre-commit hook's command line because both
# consumers read this file, and a hook that analysed less than the gate would
# pass commits the gate then refuses.
CheckOptions:
  clang-analyzer-ipa: dynamic
...
